Package: erhai-display-power
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: python3, systemd, libc6 (>= 2.34), gnome-settings-daemon (>= 50), gnome-settings-daemon (<< 51)
Description: Backlight-only display blanking for the OnePlus Pad 2 Pro
 Keeps the display link running while switching the panel backlight: the one
 led-backlight device through which the kernel drives both KTZ8868 chips. The
 service is skipped on kernels with any other backlight layout, such as one
 device per chip. A device-scoped adapter redirects GNOME Settings Daemon 50's
 display-power setter; battery management and GNOME authentication remain in
 the original distribution processes. This workaround increases screen-off
 power and does not establish display recovery from system suspend.
 .
 erhai-display-power-mode switches to GNOME's own display power path
 (standard) on kernels that recover from the display power collapse, and
 back (compat, the default). It only writes overrides -- masks and a marker
 in /etc, or in /run so that the next boot is compat again -- and changes no
 packaged file.
